AB  - Agentic AI systems are autonomous, goal-directed artificial intelligence agents capable of reasoning, planning, and acting in dynamic environments. As these systems become increasingly integrated into critical domains such as healthcare, finance, governance, and industrial automation, ensuring ethical integrity and reliable deployment is paramount. This article provides a comprehensive review of agentic AI architectures, highlighting various models ranging from rule-based and multiagent systems to reinforcement learning and hybrid frameworks. Ethical considerations, including fairness, transparency, privacy, and value alignment, are analyzed in the context of real-world applications. Deployment strategies emphasizing robustness, scalability, security, and continuous monitoring are discussed to ensure that agentic AI systems operate safely and effectively in practical environments. The paper concludes with future research directions to advance the development of trustworthy and responsible agentic AI systems, bridging technical innovation with societal impact. © 2026 IEEE.
