AB  - The design of built facilities is inherently shaped by stakeholder values; however, mechanisms for embedding these values within automated layout generation frameworks are still lacking. Existing platforms typically emphasize objective performance criteria, lacking explicit mechanisms to embed values in generation or evaluation. This work introduces Values-Driven Layout Generation and Evaluation (VALGEN), a three-stage framework for automating values-driven layout generation and assessment. Implemented on a programming platform, VALGEN generates layouts via a force-based method, computes seven design performance indicators using geometric modeling tools, and translates these into value scores based on stakeholder-defined weightages. Stakeholders can interact with results through a dedicated user interface. Testing showed that VALGEN could rapidly generate hundreds of layouts, 90% of which were unique; in a few cases, automated layouts outperformed human-designed counterparts. These findings demonstrate VALGEN's potential to merge stakeholder values with automated design workflows, enabling both scale and value alignment in layout generation.  © 2026 American Society of Civil Engineers.
