AB  - EmoLawConnect is an AI-powered matching engine for family conflict resolution that recommends lawyers by combining legal case profiles with clients' emotional preferences and value alignment. It integrates a multi-layer pipeline that processes user inputs (e.g., emotional expression, legal needs) and professional profiles (e.g., legal expertise, practice orientation). The architecture merges rule-based pre-filtering with a semantic-emotional scoring module built on matrix factorization and value-aware alignment. The prototype was evaluated through scenario-based testing and a rule-based legal-consistency proxy. Results suggest improved user-professional compatibility and trust, with potential contributions to access to justice. The approach provides a foundation for broader legal-service applications where affective or interpersonal alignment matters.  © 2025 The Authors.
