AB  - With the advancement of generative artificial intelligence (AI) technology, generative AI-based agent systems are increasingly being applied across multiple domains, and the demand for value alignment in these systems is also growing. This study employs CiteSpace bibliometric visualization analysis on 333 relevant papers from the Web of Science database between January 2015 and May 2025. Analysis of existing research reveals that current generative AI agents primarily focus on aligning and optimizing underlying language models, lacking design and optimization research for universal human value alignment across multiple application scenarios. The classification system for human values within current agent systems urgently requires systematic refinement, and their ability to achieve multi-level value alignment with users must be enhanced. By summarizing current research and identifying existing limitations, we have outlined the direction that further optimization research on generative AI digital agents in the alignment of human values should take, and propose that future research should build upon this framework to refine and enhance it. In summary, this study employs bibliometric methods to conduct a comprehensive analysis of human value alignment design and optimization in generative AI agents across three dimensions: authenticity and credibility, practical feasibility, and emotional controllability. It provides practical guidance for future research in this field. © 2026 IEEE.
