AB  - The proceedings contain 87 papers. The special focus in this conference is on Cross-Cultural Design. The topics include: Study on Style Transfer of Lingnan Manchu Window Decorative Patterns Based on SD-LoRA Technology; Touchable Sacredness: Human–AI Co-creation in Cross-Cultural Design Employing Mazu Water-Pattern Symbols for Lacquerware; AI Collaborative Innovation: Literature-Oriented Picture Book Design; Reshaping Cultural Memory Through Generative AI: Dynamic Inheritance of Minority Architectural Heritage Components; Research on Cultural Meme Genealogy Construction and Human-AI Collaborative Artistic Mural Design Based on Memetics and AIGC; Exploring Loafer Appeal Factors Through the Application of AI-Generated Technologies in the Kansei Engineering Design Process; From Prompt to Play: A Full-Process AIGC Framework and Calibration Strategies for Cantonese Culinary Game Design; A Study on the “AI-Designer-Craftsman” Collaborative Design Model Based on Yixing Zisha Craftsmanship in the Digital-Intelligence Era; Co-designing AI-Thenticity in Cross-Cultural Design: Authenticity Judgments and Trust in AI-Generated Cultural Symbols; Value Alignment and Expertise Drift: Value Differences in Manual Data Annotation Based on BERT Models; Balancing Innovation and Integrity in the Age of AI: Using Design Thinking to Guide Students in Meaningful AI Usage While Preventing Over-Reliance; Beyond Bias and Usability: Policy-Guided Inclusive Design for Cognitive and Emotional Safety in AI Digital Platforms; Survey on the Current Situation of Aesthetic Ability of Non-art and Design Major Students and Their Demand for AIGC Technology Application; interaction Empowerment and Digital Adaptation for the Elderly: A Study on Demand-Oriented Curriculum and Interaction Design in Continuing Education for Older Adults; spatial Distribution of Acoustic Treatments in Learning Environments.
