AB  - This study focuses on the application of large models in ideological and political education and proposes an automatic construction method for ideological and political teaching cases based on educational large models integrated with a chain-of-thought enhancement mechanism. This method is based on the fine-tuned educational large model LLaMA-2-Edu and introduces a chain-of-thought-driven knowledge structuring module (CoT-KSM) to simulate the teacher's conceptualization process. It decomposes abstract ideological and political concepts into multi-level cognitive chains and aligns case content with teaching objectives through a multi-task semantic alignment layer and a policy-value logic optimization network. To improve the realism and diversity of cases, the model integrates contrastive prompt tuning and cross-modal value matching mechanisms, accessing a case memory database to automatically organize textbook content, current affairs materials, and typical events. Experimental results indicate that the proposed model improves value alignment and teaching effectiveness by 17.6% and 21.3%, respectively, compared to existing educational large models.  © 2026 Copyright held by the owner/author(s).
