AB  - We introduce HPR-GenRM, a hierarchical process-level generative reward model for robust large language model (LLM) alignment in offline reinforcement learning from human feedback (RLHF) settings, unifying long-horizon reasoning with explicit step-by-step verification through a three-tier architecture. Training on 25K hierarchically-annotated instances from HelpSteer2, MATH, and CodeContests, our Llama-3-8B-based model achieves 82.3% accuracy on RM-Bench (7.2% improvement over state-of-the-art), 89.1% step accuracy on MATH-500 with error localization F1 of 0.83, and 61% relative reduction in undetected adversarial attacks. Integration into RLHF yields 58.3% win rate on AlpacaEval2 (11.1% gain) while reducing policy-level reward hacking from 15% to 5%. This work presents hierarchical process-level reasoning as an effective approach for interpretable reward modeling within offline reward labeling and quality-sensitive alignment settings. © 2026 Elsevier Ltd. All rights are reserved, including those for text and data mining, AI training, and similar technologies.
