AB  - This paper presents an enhanced methodological framework for formalizing organizational values into a computable, domain-aware ontology using Semantic Web technologies, specifically addressing Human Resource (HR) challenges in large, multi-domain research organizations. Building on our foundational Military Research Value Ontology (MRVO), we extend the framework to incorporate domain-specific value contextualization inspired by military research domains such as Multiple Rocket Launcher (MRL) systems development. The integrated HR-MRVO framework formally encodes organizational core values, domain-adapted value profiles, and individual/team value manifestations using OWL 2 DL. It operationalizes value-based HR processes through SWRL rules, SHACL constraints, and SPARQL analytics. A design-science pilot demonstrates improvements in value-alignment reporting, cross-domain talent mobility, and HR strategic alignment. The study provides a semantically grounded, HR-centric methodology for bridging abstract organizational principles with executable, domain-sensitive value management systems. © 2026 IEEE.
