AB  - Consulting has become an increasingly important avenue through which anesthesiologists apply their clinical, operational, and analytical expertise to improve healthcare systems. This chapter explores the expanding intersection of anesthesiology and healthcare consulting, detailing how physicians can lead initiatives in perioperative efficiency, cost containment, quality improvement, and data-driven decision-making. Drawing from both academic and industry perspectives, it outlines the structure and scope of perioperative consulting engagements, from OR utilization analysis and scheduling optimization to revenue cycle management, staffing models, and strategic growth planning. This chapter provides a framework for anesthesiologists interested in consulting-whether as internal advisors within their institutions or as external experts collaborating with hospital systems, management firms, or private equity organizations. It emphasizes ethical considerations, conflict-of-interest awareness, and the need for transparency and value alignment when physicians assume advisory roles. Through case examples and practical insights, readers will gain a deeper understanding of how anesthesiology's systems-based expertise uniquely positions the specialty to shape healthcare operations, policy, and strategy-cementing the anesthesiologist's identity as both clinician and consultant in a rapidly evolving healthcare landscape. © The Editor(s) (if applicable) and The Author(s), under exclusive license to Springer Nature Switzerland AG 2026.
