AB  - The doctor-patient shared decision-making model emphasizes patient safety engagement, playing a crucial role in ensuring patient safety and improving the quality and efficiency of medical services. To establish a harmonious doctor-patient relationship, achieve the high-quality development of the hospital, and enhance the quality of medical services for patients, this paper adopted the doctor-patient shared decision making model as a research framework and integrated relevant ethical theories. Based on the doctor-patient shared decision-making model and its ethical value, several countermeasures were proposed, including establishing a doctor-patient trust mechanism, promoting high-quality engagement, optimizing the information sharing system, facilitating value alignment, improving the risk communication process, and utilizing decision support tools. The aim was to meet the ethical requirements for patient safety engagement and ensure the effective implementation of doctor-patient shared decision-making, thereby promoting the establishment of a harmonious doctor-patient relationship and fostering the high-quality development of the hospital. © 2025, Editorial department of Chinese Medical Ethics. All right reserved.
