AD  - Nanjing University of Posts and Telecommunications, School of Computer Science, Nanjing, China
AB  - Evaluating the learning effectiveness of university students is essential for improving both instructional efficiency and learning quality. However, traditional evaluation methods are often hindered by high subjectivity, limited sample sizes, and negative impacts on teaching practices, which restrict their interpretability, feasibility, sustainability, and scalability. With the rapid advancement of Artificial Intelligence (AI), the emerging paradigm of "AI + Education"presents unprecedented opportunities to address these limitations. Motivated by this, the present study designs and implements an AI tutor-based learning evaluation system. Specifically, we construct a real-world classroom interaction dataset and develop a workflow for an interactive AI agent grounded in the AI tutor framework. Comparative experiments and expert evaluations demonstrate the significant effectiveness of the AI tutoring system in enhancing student engagement and fostering creative outcomes in higher education settings, particularly in tasks requiring creative problem solving. These findings provide valuable insights into the application of Large Language Models (LLMs) in education and the pedagogical potential of AI tutor agents. Furthermore, this study investigates the influence of the level of AI cognition of university students on their learning behaviors and outcomes. The results suggest that sustained use of AI tools promotes deeper technological understanding and stronger value alignment, leading to a reinforcing cycle of cognitive and behavioral development. Building upon these insights, we propose a three-dimensional AI literacy development framework, i.e., Cognition, Skills, and Ethics, to guide the design of intelligent educational tools, enhance AI literacy of students, and support the development of discipline-specific AI-driven educational resources. This framework aims to precisely address the diverse needs of different academic disciplines while offering both theoretical foundations and practical strategies for advancing intelligent education reform. © 2025 IEEE.
