AB  - With the widespread application of Large Language Models (LLMs) in various fields, ensuring their outputs align with societal moral norms has become a critical AI safety issue. To address this, this paper proposes an efficient value alignment method based on LoRA fine-tuning of the Llama3-8B model. Using a dataset of 10,000 value-aligned examples, we conducted fine-tuning and evaluated the model across four key dimensions. Experimental results demonstrate that this approach significantly enhances the model's ethical alignment and safety: safety improved by approximately 11.48%, the alignment score increased by 6.24%, and the refusal rate decreased by 10.6%. This indicates a strengthened ability to identify and reject high-risk requests, offering a promising alternative that reduces the reliance on human annotation inherent in RLHF.  © 2025 IEEE.
