AB  - The luxury industry's transformation in recent decades reflects growing integration of ethical and sustainable values due to societal pressure and evolving consumer expectations. This chapter examines ethical and sustainable co-branding as an emerging strategy in luxury, addressing demands for transparency, responsibility, and environmental commitment. Using a qualitative, multiple case study approach, it analyzes four collaborations: Burberry x The RealReal, Chantecaille x Space for Giants, Stella McCartney x Parley for the Oceans, and IWC x Laureus Sport for Good. Findings indicate that co-branding can effectively integrate sustainable practices while preserving luxury's symbolic value, expanding audiences, reinforcing brand authenticity, and supporting the Sustainable Development Goals (SDGs). Challenges include the risk of greenwashing, value alignment between partners, and equity in collaboration. © 2026, IGI Global Scientific Publishing. All rights reserved.
