AB  - In the era of the digital economy, high-quality Environmental, Social, and Governance (ESG) information disclosure constitutes the cornerstone of trust in electronic commerce. However, the significant divergence in traditional ESG ratings creates a "trust deficit"that hinders market efficiency. To address the "granularity deficit"and "black box"limitations of static evaluation models, this paper proposes a Multi-Head Attention Dual-Branch Neural Network. Unlike conventional deep learning architectures, this model functions as a semantic prism, autonomously capturing long-range dependencies within unstructured disclosure texts. By assigning differential weights to substantive versus ceremonial rhetoric, it establishes a novel "Semantics-Value Alignment"paradigm for precise evaluation. Empirical results on 8,200 listed companies demonstrate that the proposed method achieves an accuracy of 0.89 and an F1-score of 0.87, significantly outperforming baselines like Convolutional Neural Networks (CNNs) and XGBoost. This study not only provides an interpretable tool for automated divergence traceability but also enhances the governance intelligence of the digital business ecosystem.  © 2025 IEEE.
