AB  - This study examines the impact of organizational AI capability on employees' cognitive work ability in the tourism and hospitality industry. This study assesses the mediating role of AI ethics and the moderating role of value alignment in shaping the cognitive work ability of employees in the tourism and hospitality industry. The data was collected from 429 tourism and hospitality services firms in China. We utilized AMOS 24 and SPSS 23 to assess and evaluate the research model. By utilizing socio-technical system (STS) theory, the findings suggest that AI capability positively influences AI ethics, which enhances cognitive work ability among tourism and hospitality employees. The study further highlights the crucial role of value alignment, demonstrating that higher value alignment strengthens the relationship between AI capability and AI ethics, leading to improved employee engagement and cognitive functions. Conversely, this relationship weakens at lower levels of value alignment. This research contributes to STS theory by emphasizing the importance of integrating ethical considerations in AI deployment, challenging the assumption that technological sophistication inherently leads to ethical excellence. For managers, the study recommends prioritizing comprehensive AI ethics policies, employee training, and fostering a collaborative culture to align AI practices with ethical standards. © 2025 Informa UK Limited, trading as Taylor & Francis Group.
