AB  - Authentic leadership (AL) promotes self-awareness, transparency, and value alignment. For female leaders, practising AL presents unique challenges due to gender stereotypes that can undermine their perceived authenticity and authority. These obstacles often lead to impostor syndrome and reduced self-efficacy. Female leaders must balance authenticity with organisational expectations and foster inclusive cultures that value diverse perspectives. Despite these challenges, authentic female leaders can drive significant positive change, fostering innovation and enhancing team performance. Supporting female leaders through mentorship and professional development is crucial for promoting an inclusive workplace and leveraging the strengths of authentic leadership. © The Editors and Contributing Authors Severally 2025.
