AB  - This paper introduces the 3×2A Strategy, a conceptual framework for societal adaptation to Generative AI (GenAI) and large language models (LLMs). It maps six strategic dimensions—Automation, Augmentation, Alliance, Alignment, Adaptation, and Accountability—critical for fostering human–AI synergy. We apply the framework to education, healthcare, and scientific research, illustrating its role in guiding responsible integration and governance. The 3×2A Strategy contributes to foundational discourse on AI alignment and sociotechnical transformation, offering a structured approach to aligning GenAI advancements with societal needs, institutional structures, and long-term resilience. ©2025 by Computer Science Journal of Moldova.
