AB  - The ethical, economic, social, and regulatory issues continue to mount with the increasing use of autonomous AI agents across heterogeneous areas of social value. This chapter sets out a framework through which the multidimensional effects of autonomous AI agents in different specific areas of social value can be analyzed. Applying this adaptive impact aggregation, coupled with validation through the collection of empirical data and simulation involving hundreds of agents on various levels of governance, an overall social score was achieved. In this regard, the maximum effect measured 89% for participatory governance, 91% for ethical alignment, and at least 35% for economic disruption. These agents performed 61% better than the high-autonomy agents without restriction. Stakeholder engagement and governance will enable AI alignment. This framework enables AI developers, policy makers, and other stakeholders to act on scaling, measuring, and using AI tools in an ethical manner while the automated systems become transparent, fair, and accountable.  © 2025 IEEE.
