TI  - HicAgent: Hierarchical Iterative Cooperative Learning Reward Generation Guided by a Large Model
PY  - 2025
T2  - 2025 IEEE 3rd International Conference on Big Data and Data Mining, BDDM 2025 - Proceedings
DO  - 10.1109/BDDM68348.2025.11442170
UR  - https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/105037431618?origin=resultslist
AD  - College of Artificial Intelligence, Changchun University of Science and Technology, Changchun, China
AB  - Reward design plays a fundamental role in reinforcement learning (RL), yet it typically requires extensive domain expertise and significant manual effort. In conventional RL paradigms, the construction of reward functions is heavily dependent on expert knowledge, making the process time-consuming and labor-intensive. Recent advancements in large language models (LLMs) have introduced new opportunities for automating and optimizing reward design, owing to their powerful semantic understanding, code synthesis, and contextual reasoning capabilities. In this paper, we present HicAgent, a hierarchical-iterative-cooperative framework for automated reward design. The proposed framework integrates environmental perception, dynamic feedback, and multi-agent collaboration to support adaptive and interpretable reward generation. HicAgent incorporates key components such as zero-shot reward generation, evolutionary search, and iterative reward optimization, effectively addressing core challenges including reward sparsity, reward hacking, and multi-objective balance. Experimental results demonstrate that HicAgent surpasses four baseline methods, achieving success rates of 90.8% in robotic manipulation tasks, 87.2% in autonomous navigation, and 83.5% in game control environments. These results validate the framework generality, efficiency, and interpretability in complex RL settings. © 2025 IEEE.
