AB  - This opinion paper argues that current approaches to Educational Developer (EdDever) professional development in UK higher education inadequately address the complex challenges these Third Space Professionals face. Critical to the realisation of institutions’ student-facing missions, the CPD of this staff group matters to all who teach/support HE learning. Traditional skills-first frameworks fail to acknowledge the fundamental importance of values alignment in enabling authentic practice while sustaining personal wellbeing in increasingly neoliberal institutional environments. We propose a values-first approach to EdDever CPD, centred on a ‘Unique Values Proposition’ (UVP), supported by extrapreneurial capabilities to enable EdDevers to create value-aligned networks across organisational boundaries. This paper challenges the sector to recognise EdDevers’ critical contributions and embrace values-first development approaches that sustain both their effectiveness and wellbeing in increasingly metric-driven environments. © 2025 Informa UK Limited, trading as Taylor & Francis Group.
