AB  - As artificial intelligence (AI) becomes embedded in software applications, from chatbots to semi-Autonomous agents, ensuring these systems uphold human values presents a significant challenge distinct from aligning the underlying AI models. Whilst much attention has focused on making AI models safe, the software systems that orchestrate and expose these models introduce additional complexity where value misalignment can emerge through interface design, adaptive behaviour, and user interaction patterns. This paper presents a vision for AI-driven systems that are aligned with human values by design, as traditional software engineering approaches are insufficient for dynamic, adaptive AI-driven systems. We propose the Value Alignment in Software Systems (VASS) framework built on five interconnected pillars: operationalising values into measurable indicators, architecturally integrating values, building in auditability, enabling participatory alignment, and providing accessible tools for diverse developers. As AI-driven software becomes society's primary AI interface, integrating value alignment as a core software engineering practice is essential to ensure these systems remain trustworthy and accountable. © 2025 IEEE.
