TI  - Facilitating AI Alignment: Weak-to-Strong Generalization with Debate Mechanisms in Language Models
PY  - 2024
T2  - Australasian Conference on Robotics and Automation, ACRA
VL  - 2024-November
UR  - https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85219547424?origin=resultslist
AB  - As AI systems increasingly surpass human-level performance in complex tasks, aligning them with human values becomes critical. We present a novel framework for aligning language models through weak-to-strong generalization, where a strong model facilitates a weaker one via a formal facilitation function Φ. This approach enables capability transfer without extensive training data. We incorporate debate mechanisms, leveraging adversarial dynamics to enhance alignment by evaluating and refining model explanations. Strong and weak models provide explanations for their decisions, evaluated by a judge, fostering transparency and interpretability essential for trust and alignment with human values. Experiments across complex tasks, including natural language processing benchmarks and strategic game scenarios, demonstrate significant improvements in model performance and alignment through our facilitation-based approach. Our analysis offers insights into model alignment in decision-making and the potential for scalable oversight of advanced AI systems. These findings suggest that our framework enhances model capabilities and provides a promising direction for developing robust, aligned AI systems capable of handling increasingly complex tasks while remaining aligned with human values. © 2024 Australasian Robotics and Automation Association. All rights reserved.
