AB  - Large Language Models act as an all-inclusive ground for engagement. However, the output of these models is not always aligned with the correct human preferences or values. This can produce a large range of inappropriate and offensive content. In human culture/society, proverbs act as a way to transmit and shape human values and behavior. In this research, we experiment to determine whether or not proverbs can play the same role for LLMs in transmitting and aligning to human values. Additionally, we research to determine how we can prompt LLMs to generate their own set of rules for categories of human values and use that as a means to align future-generated content to said values. © 2024 SPIE.
