AB  - • Providing and maintaining the nation's nuclear warheads throughout the product life cycle requires operating and maintaining an extensive and diverse range of infrastructure assets • The asset management standard is a series of three standards for asset management and the asset management standard is based on a set of four fundamentals - value, alignment, leadership and assurance. • Asset management must cover the entire asset life cycle from design, installation and commissioning through to operations and decommissioning. • AWE's Site Optimisation Plan that interprets and translates the corporate business strategy and summarises it into a 10-year plan with the first two years in sufficient detail to inform and set the annual budget round. • AWE has developed a new approach to managing its infrastructure that intrinsically connects operating assets with the wider corporate business strategy. • It is now developing leading and lagging indicators that are aligned to its asset management objectives and upgrading the system it uses for computerised maintenance management. © 2018 Nuclear Institute. All rights reserved.
