AB  - The emerging field of value awareness engineering claims that software agents and systems should be value-aware, i.e. they should be able to explicitly reason about the value-alignment of their actions. Existing approaches characterize values in various ways, from which we defend the recently introduced context-based value taxonomies, which allow a very rich context-dependent value representation while providing alignment explainability. We propose further work in the area, that would strive mainly on the feasibility for a system to learn value taxonomies from streams of value-aware preferences (using CEP rule learning), so the result is human-readable and representative of a complex value system. © 2023, The Author(s), under exclusive license to Springer Nature Switzerland AG.
