AB  - The article is about the computer-aided modelling of the relability behavior of fault-tolerant computer systems. The reasons for and the effects of the appearance of multiprocessor, multicomputer systems are analyzed, the traditional hardware redundance structures are surveyed. For the design of a highly reliable system, the reliability features of the system have to be characterized. Markov modelling provides the basis for the developed Reliability Estimating Program Package (REPP). The REPP can be very well used at the testing of different redundant structures. The described model is able to take into consideration the different behavior of spare modules and degradation systems, the unsuccessful adjustment, further the effect of transient errors and the corrigibility.
