AB  - This paper is devoted to the study of imaging processing and motion compensation of C-band inverse synthetic aperture radar (C-ISAR). Motion compensation is approached in two steps: the range alignment and initial phase compensation. The method of cross-correlation alignment combined with peak value alignment is proposed in range alignment and proved to be effective. Dominant Scatterer algorithm is used in phase compensation. PGA autofocus algorithm is tested in ISAR imaging. Finally, an improved CLEAN algorithm is used in ISAR imaging and post-image processing.
